  exhibitName: Counter of the City Council
  description: 'This elaborately decorated writing casket was used by a city scribe,
    a professional responsible for producing official records, legal documents, and
    correspondence. The box contains compartments designed to hold quills, inkpots,
    sealing wax, and other essential writing tools. Its raised lid also served as
    a portable writing surface. '
